161	// item is born carrying a `### Context`, and the hand-off writes Context again — so
162	// an append leaves TWO sections of that name, while the session is told to read "the
163	// issue's Context section", singular. The one it reads first is then the tick's birth
164	// note and the binding scope is in the other, which fails silently whichever section
165	// the agent picks. It also grows: an item re-queued through hand-off twice carried a
